From d6fcc25b22710aa76f5323da80f5526301fdec89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan McCallum <apt-install-coffee@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:55:59 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 145/145] v7.2: port Sky1 DRM display stack to updated DRM APIs

v7.2 landed several DRM flag-day changes that the linlon-dp and trilin
DPTX/MST drivers must follow:

- Atomic callbacks and helpers now take struct drm_atomic_commit instead
  of struct drm_atomic_state; rename accordingly across the display stack
  (and drm_atomic_state_put -> drm_atomic_commit_put).
- The DRM_COLOR_FORMAT_* bitmask macros were removed; display_info.color_formats
  is now encoded as BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_*). Add a small compat shim
  with identical bit positions.
- drm_private_state_funcs gained atomic_create_state and
  drm_atomic_private_obj_init() dropped its initial-state argument; give
  each Sky1 private object an atomic_create_state callback.
- drm_panel_init() removed in favour of devm_drm_panel_alloc().
- dedup drm/Kconfig: v7.2 moved all driver source lines into the sorted
  block, so only add the cix/sky1 entries there.
